      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the presence of a cervical esophagostomy, a median sternotomy may jeopardize the stoma, risk mediastinal or sternal infection, and potentially compromise future esophageal operations. Coronary artery bypass grafting was performed using a modified bilateral thoracotomy before esophageal reconstruction in a patient with cervical esophagostomy. The surgical technique is described with a review of the relevant literature."},
